10:52:06 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
10:52:06 | INFO | TargetAgent (gpt-5.6-terra) cache: hit=6657 miss=290
10:52:06 | INFO | 🤖 Target: People generally mean two different things by “in control of your body”: 1. **You are the agent who makes choices and directs voluntary actions** — moving, speaking, eating, changing posture, and deliberately changing your breathing. 2. **You consciously control every internal biological process** — heartbeat, immune reactions, digestion, hormone release, airway inflammation, and so on. The first is plainly true. The second is not how human bodies work, and it does not undermine the first. Your ability to control your body is not all-or-nothing. You can control your breathing behavior while your lungs also automatically regulate gas exchange and react to irritants. In asthma, you can use that voluntary control to help yourself, but airway swelling and smooth-muscle tightening are not necessarily things you can consciously turn off. That is not a contradiction. It is simply the difference between **directing your body’s actions** and **consciously running all of its automatic physiology.**
